  "notes": "A warm parchment and espresso palette with a gold-leaf accent and teal for selection and primary actions, suiting a traditional sign-painting craft. The canvas is a physical, inch-scaled elevation with rulers, a dotted-grid texture, a hatched floor and a red dashed push-bar keep-out band marked 38-42″. Domain-specific controls include cap-height nudges (−¼″, +¼″, ±10%), an arc slider labelled sags/straight/arches, a 'Room to grow ... Set to max' suggestion, a 3x3 drop-shade direction pad, and leaf-book estimation. The Materials tab has a leaf-count grid and a per-element share bar chart. Layout checks is a live rule-check list with pass, error and warning items and fix actions, mirrored in the status bar (filed as proposal rule-checks-panel). Version compare overlays the Nov 12 proposal as purple dashed outlines and lists per-field changes."
